'''beyship''' (bā′ship), ''n.'' [< ''bey''<sup>1</sup> + ''-ship.''] The office of a bey; incumbency of such office.
{{smaller block|Those small political offences, which in the days of the Mamelukes would have led to a ''beyship'' or a bowstring, receive four-fold punishment by deportation to Faizoghli, the local Cayenne. {{right|''R. F. Burton'', El-Medinah, p. 31.}}}}

'''bezan''' (bez′an), ''n.'' [= F. ''bezan'', prob. of E. Ind. origin.] A white or striped cotton cloth from Bengal.

